 take a step back  and not make the man bon jovi  but that's just my take she says  of course that's how that's just my  opinion you know  don't don't kill the messenger  here's the thing  she's right  that's a weird thing to say  but tomi lahren is right  and she's right  for several reasons  the first is  what's he done  well let's be honest we all know what  happened  two people are dead kyle ridden house  was acquitted  now we could argue all day long whether  or not you think it was self-defense  whether you think he should be here but  those arguments no longer really matter  okay kyle rittenhouse  faced the jury  he had his defense  we had the prosecutors  defense prevailed kyle rittenhouse was  acquitted  that's the end of that so we're not even  going to get into that  but two people are dead and we know that  he killed him the court says it's in  self-defense so we have to accept that  and now he's a hero  like now they're lifting him up now they  gave him a speaking gig  now i'll be perfectly honest with you i  don't know what he said i didn't listen  to it i have no interest in listening to  it i don't care what he has to say  although we do know  that he did say in an interview after  the acquittal that you know people  shouldn't be praising him for this  i guess he's i guess he's okay with it  now  but either way laryn's point i think i  don't want to put words in her mouth but  i think what she's trying to get at is  why  what's the longevity  of kyle rittenhouse  what is he actually doing to further the  conservative cause  so the answer to that question would  obviously be  nothing  not a thing  and of course turning point is supposed  to be about these conservatives who are  out there making a difference pushing  their horrible conservative policies on  us spitting out giving us new  conservative talking points  but that's not what kyle rittenhouse is  he's not a political operative  i mean he's a  kid he's a kid that's now gotten swept  up into all of this  and honestly  i don't think he understands it either i  don't think he knows where he's going  with this  does he have a future in the  conservative movement  does kyle rittenhouse have a shelf life  and that's the big point that tomi  lahren herself is attempting to make  think of it this way  i pointed this out actually on fair and  balanced as well  um the mccloskeys right the st louis gun  couple we all remember them right  what what are they doing now  they were conservative heroes  heck they had a speaking spot  at the gop convention last year where  are they now are they still these  conservative rising stars i know i know  the the guy was gonna run for senate and  i don't think that went very well for  him  i don't even know if that's still  happening  because nobody cares about the  mccloskeys anymore  and the same thing will eventually  happen to kyle rittenhouse  you know maybe  you know the gun rights organizations  will try to use him as a poster child  maybe he'll do that maybe he won't  that's all pure speculation at this  point to be honest we don't know what he  will or will not do with this newfound  fame  but one thing we can pretty much all  come to the same conclusion on  is that based on others who've been in  this situation before the fame doesn't  last  the spotlights fade  they disappear and people will forget  except the families affected  who this individual is and they won't  care anymore  and i would like to think that that's  what tomi lahren was getting at  but i also think  there could be a degree of jealousy  there right  and let's face it a couple years ago  tomi lahren was the it girl right  she was the one everybody was clamoring  for she was the one making the headlines  she was the one out there  helping  craft the direction of the republican  party  a lot of people forgot she existed  so maybe  maybe and this is you know to to pull a  laryn that's just my opinion maybe  she's a little jealous of having to  share the 